# A card that fills up in the middle of a job does not hold up the ST: with
# 2 KB left on the card, PRFILES still prints our ESC/P pages (2962 bytes) to
# the end, and the RP answers every block (the hook drops nothing). The RP
# writes what fits, says the write failed, and deletes the job: no part of it
# stays on the card, and the menu says it was lost. The RP tells a full card
# by its free space, which EmuMD always gives as 16 GB: here the job is lost
# because "the card failed", on a real full card because "the card is full".
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/escp.st
text "Machine +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 1500
cardfull 2048
key e
wait 100
key 0x01
wait 900
key 0x39
hookdone 2962 3000
log "printer: write failed" 100
log "printer: job 00000001 lost: the card (is full|failed), deleted" 100
wait 600
cardnone PRINTER/*.PRN
cardnone PRINTER/*.TMP
hookstate
